  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Below average temperatures expected through Tuesday, \nwith frost possible tonight. \n\nCanadian high pressure will move from the Central Great Lakes to the \neastern Great Lakes region tonight through Tuesday. The ridge of \nhigh pressure will reach western NY late tonight. Calm winds and \nmostly clear skies will support good radiational cooling late \ntonight into Tuesday morning. Low temperatures are expected to fall \nto the mid to upper 30s across most of the region, with the low 40s \nnear the lakes shores. Low to mid 30s are expected across the North \nCountry and Cattaraugus and Allegany counties. \n\nPatchy to areas of frost are expected across sheltered valleys away \nfrom the Lakes late tonight. The window for frost development will \nbe short, as the ridge of high pressure will not move into western \nNY until late. The highest confidence for frost development is \nacross sheltered valleys and interior locations of Chautauqua, \nsouthern Erie, and Wyoming counties, where a Frost Advisory has \nbeen issued. Elsewhere within areas still in the growing season,\nfrost coverage will be less widespread. \n\nThe cool airmass will remain across the region Tuesday with \nhigh temperatures in the mid to upper 50s. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Warmer conditions return mid-week with periods of \nshowers through the end of the work week. \n\nA surface ridge will move east of the forecast area Tuesday night. \nThe pressure gradient will tighten while warm air advection \nincreases across the eastern Great Lakes region through Wednesday. \nBreezy with winds gusts up to 30 mph northeast of Lake Erie. \nTemperatures will rebound into the mid to upper 60s on Wednesday. A \nseries of shortwave troughs and frontal boundaries will move across \nthe forecast area through Friday. Brief periods of showers are \npossible, however confidence is low on timing and amounts at this \ntime.",
